m=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured HashiCorp raft Go module: leader/follower replication, elections, persistence interfaces, snapshots and FSM/client completion. External caller FSM and durable backends are injected; in-repository implementations are not assumed externalized.',protocol_contexts=['One node current term and configuration','One leader tenure commitment object','Indexed replicated log and snapshot boundary'],external_interfaces=['Apply/ApplyLog futures','Transport RPC and pipeline','LogStore, StableStore, SnapshotStore','FSM callbacks'],ownership=['Main Raft loop owns role/configuration and log admission','Per-peer goroutines own replication progress','FSM worker owns callback execution'],source_ids=['restart','transport_interface','fsm_contract','client_apply']),activities=A,behaviors=B,facts=F,surfaces=[dict(entry_point='Raft.appendEntries commit bound',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_follower_append','B_replicate'],reason='Can a legal bounded request commit a retained divergent suffix? Ordinary backtracking is counterevidence, and producer history remains unresolved.',source_ids=['follower_accept','request_bounds','replication_reply'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft.appendEntries storage-error suffix',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['B_follower_append','B_history'],reason='What responsibility applies after truncation succeeds and StoreLogs fails with cached lastLog unchanged?',source_ids=['follower_accept'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='Raft administrative restore/recovery',disposition='deferred',reason='Caller-authorized history replacement and disaster recovery need separate contract analysis; ordinary snapshot transfer is mapped.',source_ids=['client_apply'],high_consequence=True)],core_overview=dict(status='usable',core_gaps=[],open_details=['Follower commit-boundary producer/history premise remains unresolved.','Storage failure, membership identity replacement and snapshot-retained-suffix variants remain open.','Administrative history replacement, legacy protocol variations and transport fast-path concurrency require deeper review.'],rationale='Representative formation and authority lifecycles, their shared history/eligibility mechanisms, old-work handling and asynchronous consumption have been traced. Usable is a navigation judgment, not correctness or exhaustive coverage.',formation=path('Leader stamps admitted commands with term/index and stores them. Local storage and successful peer append/snapshot replies report match indexes into a tenure-owned object. Latest voters supply majority support, gated by a current-term entry. commitCh consumption publishes commitment, commits configurations and queues inflight logs. Replication advertises commitment; follower validates term/previous history, reconciles received conflicts and selects a local application bound. FSM queueing and callback completion are separate; commands complete their futures after callbacks.',['B_client','B_formation','B_replicate','B_follower_append','B_apply'],['F_leader_commit','F_follower_commit']),context=path('Contact timeout starts eligible voter campaigning, optionally via pre-vote. Durable term/vote records, membership and lexicographic log freshness govern voting; campaign-local channels aggregate granted votes. New leadership creates a new commitment object and no-op. Higher terms, lease failure or committed removal end authority. Leadership transfer catches a selected peer up then triggers a transfer-marked campaign. Leader exit stops replication and fails pending futures without promising their entries cannot survive.',['B_election','B_leader_context','B_membership','B_history'],[]),connection=path('Log freshness protects the history carried into new authority; persistence and snapshot restoration retain history across restart. A new tenure does not reuse the old quorum tracker: old replies reference old objects, while preserved log entries require fresh support reaching a new-term entry. Configuration controls both votes and match eligibility; new changes wait for previous commitment and current-term commitment. Followers preserve matching prefixes and reconcile received conflicts; prior queued application is not undone by leader transitions. The adequacy of the follower commit bound is a local unresolved relationship rather than assumed safety.',['B_election','B_leader_context','B_membership','B_history','B_recovery','B_follower_append','B_apply'],['F_leader_commit','F_follower_commit'])))
